1: \section{The free stress-tensor trace}
2: \label{app:gten}
3: 
4: This appendix gives the calculation behind theorem~\ref{thm:gten} in full, and
5: records how it is verified.
6: 
7: \paragraph{The stress tensor.}
8: For a $p$-form with field strength $F$ of rank $p$ in $d$ dimensions, the free
9: stress tensor takes the form
10: \begin{equation}
11: T_{\mu\nu}
12:  = \frac{1}{(p-1)!}\,F_{\mu\alpha_2\dots\alpha_p}
13:    F_\nu{}^{\alpha_2\dots\alpha_p}
14:  - c\,\eta_{\mu\nu}\,\langle F,F\rangle,
15: \label{eq:stress}
16: \end{equation}
17: where $c$ is an improvement coefficient. Different conventions in the literature
18: fix $c$ differently; the point of what follows is that the conclusion does not
19: depend on it.
20: 
21: \paragraph{The trace.}
22: Taking the trace of \eqref{eq:stress} with $\eta^{\mu\nu}$, the first term gives
23: $\langle F,F\rangle$ up to normalisation and the second gives
24: $-cd\,\langle F,F\rangle$, so
25: \begin{equation}
26: T^\mu{}_\mu = (1 - cd)\,\langle F,F\rangle .
27: \label{eq:trace}
28: \end{equation}
29: Whatever $c$ is, the trace is a multiple of the single scalar
30: $\langle F,F\rangle$. There is no other quadratic Lorentz scalar available: the
31: only way to contract two copies of a five-form into a scalar is the full
32: contraction.
33: 
34: \paragraph{The vanishing.}
35: Here $p = 5$ and $d = 10$, so $F$ is a middle-degree form of \emph{odd} degree in
36: an even-dimensional space. Consider the top form $F \wedge F$. Interchanging the
37: two factors of a $q$-form costs a sign $(-1)^{q^2} = (-1)^q$, which for $q = 5$
38: is $-1$; hence $F\wedge F = -F\wedge F$ and $F \wedge F \equiv 0$ identically,
39: for every five-form whatsoever.
40: 
41: Now $\langle F, \star F\rangle\,\mathrm{vol} \propto F \wedge F$, so
42: $\langle F, \star F\rangle = 0$. On either eigenspace of the star,
43: $\star F = \pm F$, giving
44: \begin{equation}
45: \langle F, F \rangle
46:  = \pm\,\langle F, \star F\rangle
47:  = 0 .
48: \end{equation}
49: By \eqref{eq:trace} the free stress tensor is traceless, for any improvement
50: coefficient. Consequently $\operatorname{Tr}(\tau)$ contributes nothing at field
51: degree two and first contributes at degree four.
52: 
53: \paragraph{Scope of the argument.}
54: The derivation uses only self-duality (or anti-self-duality) and the parity of
55: the form degree. It does not use the detailed form of the free dynamics, the
56: choice of improvement term, or the overall normalisation. That robustness is why
57: we regard the input as settled, and why the remaining question for review is
58: narrow: whether the intended free theory and stress convention are the ones fixed
59: in appendix~\ref{app:conventions}.
60: 
61: \paragraph{Computational verification.}
62: A dedicated test module re-derives the statement from the five-form and the
63: Hodge star alone, importing none of the flow machinery. It checks:
64: \begin{enumerate}\itemsep2pt
65: \item $\star^2 = +\starSquared$, without which the eigenspace decomposition is
66:       not the one assumed;
67: \item $\langle F,F\rangle = 0$ on self-dual samples, at eight seeds;
68: \item $\langle F,F\rangle = 0$ on \emph{anti}-self-dual samples, which the
69:       argument predicts equally and which would fail if the vanishing were an
70:       artefact of the projector rather than of the wedge identity;
71: \item the control: $\langle F,F\rangle \neq 0$ on an unprojected five-form. This
72:       is the test that gives the other three their content, since a quantity that
73:       vanished identically would satisfy them all vacuously;
74: \item the conclusion at four primes;
75: \item agreement with the production leading-degree table, read once and only to
76:       be checked against the independent derivation.
77: \end{enumerate}
78: 
79: \paragraph{A correction worth recording.}
80: An earlier version of the control called the projector routine with an argument
81: believed to select the anti-self-dual space, when in fact that argument selects
82: Lorentzian versus Euclidean signature. The apparent non-vanishing it reported was
83: a Euclidean projector, where $\star^2 = -1$ and the eigenspace decomposition is

